(a) The second screen presented on the approved device shall include the entire text of the law that is
the subject of the referendum petition.
3194 (b) An individual may not advance to the third screen until the individual clicks a link at the bottom of
the second screen stating, "By clicking here, I attest that I have read and understand the entire text of
the law that is the subject of the referendum petition."
3198 (4)
(a) The third screen presented on the approved device shall include a statement indicating whether
persons gathering signatures for the referendum petition may be paid for gathering signatures.
3201 (b) An individual may not advance to the fourth screen until the individual clicks a link at the bottom
of the third screen stating, "By clicking here, I attest that I have read and understand the information
presented on this screen."
3204 (5) The fourth screen presented on the approved device shall include the following statement, followed
by links where the individual may click "yes" or "no":
3206 "I have personally read the entirety of each statement presented on this device;
3207 I am personally signing this referendum petition;
3208 I am registered to vote in Utah; and
3209 All information I enter on this device, including my residence and post office address, is
accurate.
3211
- 99 -

HB0170 compared with HB0170S01
It is a class A misdemeanor for an individual to sign a referendum petition with a name other
than the individual's own name, or to knowingly sign the individual's name more than once for
the same referendum petition, or to sign a referendum petition when the individual knows that the
individual is not a registered voter.
3215 Do you wish to continue and sign this referendum petition?"
3216 (6)
(a) If the individual clicks "no" in response to the question described in Subsection (5), the next screen
shall include the following statement, "Thank you for your time. Please return this device to the
signature-gatherer."
3219 (b) If the individual clicks "yes" in response to the question described in Subsection (5), the website, or
the application that accesses the website, shall take the signature-gatherer and the individual signing
the referendum petition through the signature process described in Section 20A-21-201.
3222 Section 27. Section 63G-30-102 is amended to read:
3223 63G-30-102. Public notice classifications and requirements.
3225 (1) A public body or a government official that is required to provide a class A notice:
3226 (a) shall publish the public notice on the Utah Public Notice Website;
3227 (b) shall publish the public notice on the public body's or government official's official website, if the
public body or government official:
3229 (i) maintains an official website; and
3230 (ii) has an annual operating budget of $250,000 or more; and
3231 (c) except as provided in Subsection (4), and subject to Subsection (5), post the public notice in
connection with the affected area as follows:
3233 (i) if the affected area is a municipality with a population of less than 2,000, in a public location in or
near the affected area that is reasonably likely to be seen by residents of the affected area;
3236 (ii) if the affected area is a proposed municipality with a population of less than 2,000, in a public
location in or near the affected area that is reasonably likely to be seen by residents of the affected
area;
3239 (iii) if the affected area is an area other than an area described in Subsections (1)(c)(i), (1)(c)(ii), or (1)
(c)(iv) through (viii), in a public location in or near the affected area that is reasonably likely to be
seen by:
3242 (A) residents of the affected area; or
- 100 -

HB0170 compared with HB0170S01
3243 (B) if there are no residents within the affected area, individuals who pass through or near the affected
area;
3245 (iv) if the affected area is a county, in a public location within the county that is reasonably likely to be
seen by residents of the county;
3247 (v) if the affected area is a municipality with a population of 2,000 or more, or a proposed municipality
with a population of 2,000 or more, in a public location within the municipality or proposed
municipality that is reasonably likely to be seen by residents of the municipality or proposed
municipality;
3251 (vi) if the affected area is a public street, on or adjacent to the public street;
3252 (vii) if the affected area is an easement:
3253 (A) on or adjacent to the easement; or
3254 (B) in a public location that is reasonably likely to be seen by persons who are likely to be impacted by
the easement;[ {[} or]
3256 (viii) if the affected area is an interlocal entity, within, or as applicable near, each jurisdiction that is
part of the interlocal entity, in accordance with the provisions of this Subsection (1) that apply to
that jurisdiction[.] ; or
3259 (ix) if the affected area is a school district, in a public location within the school district that is
reasonably likely to be seen by residents of the school district.
3261 (2) Subject to Subsection (5), a public body or a government official that is required to provide a class
B notice shall:
3263 (a) comply with the requirements described in Subsection (1) for a class A notice;
3264 (b) if a statute, county ordinance, or municipal ordinance requires that the notice be provided for
a designated geographic area, mail or otherwise deliver the public notice or a notice summary
statement to each residence within, and, in accordance with Subsection (3), to each owner of real
property located within, the designated geographic area; and
3269 (c) if a statute, county ordinance, or municipal ordinance requires that the notice be provided to one or
more designated persons or real property owners, mail or otherwise deliver the public notice or a
notice summary statement, in accordance with Subsection (3), to each designated person and real
property owner.
3273 (3) When providing notice to a real property owner under Subsection (2)(b) or (c), the public body or
government official shall:
- 101 -

HB0170 compared with HB0170S01
3275 (a) use the current residential or business address of the real property owner;
3276 (b) if the public body or government official is not reasonably able to obtain the address described in
Subsection (3)(a), use the last known address of the real property owner that the public body or
government official is able to obtain via a reasonable inquiry into public records; or
3280 (c) if the public body or government official is not reasonably able to obtain an address described in
Subsection (3)(a) or (b), post the notice on the real property.
3282 (4) A government official, a public body, or any other body that is required to post notice under
Subsection (1) is not required to comply with Subsection (1)(c) if:
3284 (a) the affected area is the state;
3285 (b) the body is a specified body, as defined in Section 52-4-103;
3286 (c) the public body is the Legislature or a public body within the state legislative branch; or
3288 (d) the government official is required to post the notice on behalf of a body described in Subsection (4)
(b) or (c).
3290 (5) If a statute, ordinance, or rule requires a public body or government official to provide notice for a
period of time:
3292 (a) in relation to posting the notice on the Utah Public Notice Website, the requirement is not violated
due to temporary technological issues that interrupt the posting, unless the posting is interrupted for
more than 25% of the required posting time;
3295 (b) in relation to posting the notice in a physical location, the requirement is fulfilled if:
3296 (i) the notice is posted at or, except to the extent prohibited by law, before the beginning of the period
of time;
3298 (ii) the public body or government official does not remove the posting before the end of the period of
time; and
3300 (iii) until the end of the period of time, the public body or government official:
3301 (A) periodically verifies that the notice remains in place; and
3302 (B) replaces the notice within a reasonable time after discovering that the notice has been removed or
damaged; and
3304 (c) in relation to mailing, sending, or otherwise delivering notice to a person, the mailing is made at or,
except to the extent prohibited by law, before, the beginning of the period of time.
3306 Section 28. Effective date.
Effective Date.
- 102 -

HB0170 compared with HB0170S01
This bill takes effect on May 6, 2026.
